# Why a pipeline failed. One request per failing test (`test`), one per
# failed job (`job`), one over everything (`tests`, `jobs`, `diff`, `mr`).
# Format: https://github.com/chussenot/judgment/blob/main/docs/reference/jud-format.md
apiVersion: jud/v1
kind: Rubric
metadata:
  name: failed-job-triage
  minor: 4
  version: 1
  description: Whether a failing test or job is caused by the change under review, and what kind of failure it is.
spec:
  questions:
    test_caused_by_change:
      type: noul
      when: test
      instructions: >-
        Given `test.failure` and the files in `diff.changed`, is this test
        failing because of the change under review?
      criteria:
        true: the failure names, exercises or depends on code the diff changes
        false: the failure is in code the diff does not touch, or is an environment or timing problem
    test_flaky:
      type: noul
      when: test
      instructions: >-
        Does `test.failure` look like a flaky test: a timeout, a race, a
        network or resource error, rather than a wrong result?
      criteria:
        true: timeouts, connection refused, port in use, ordering or timing assertions
        false: a deterministic assertion on a value, a compile error, a missing symbol
    job_cause:
      type: choice
      when: job
      instructions: What made the job in `job.trace_tail` fail?
      criteria:
        test_failure: one or more tests failed
        build_error: compilation, type checking or packaging failed
        infrastructure: a runner, network, registry, quota or permission problem
        configuration: a missing variable, secret, file or tool
        timeout: the job or a step exceeded its time limit
        unknown: the tail does not say
    job_caused_by_change:
      type: noul
      when: job
      instructions: >-
        Given `job.trace_tail` and `diff.changed`, did the change under
        review cause this job to fail?
      criteria:
        true: the trace names files, tests or symbols the diff changes
        false: the trace names an infrastructure, configuration or unrelated problem
    pipeline_verdict:
      type: choice
      when: pipeline
      instructions: >-
        Over `tests`, `jobs` and `diff`, what should the author do first?
      criteria:
        fix_change: fix the code or tests this change touched
        retry: retry the pipeline; the failures look transient
        fix_pipeline: fix the pipeline configuration or environment
        unclear: the evidence does not say
  policy:
    test_caused_by_change:
      threshold: 0.6
    test_flaky:
      threshold: 0.6
    job_cause:
      confidence: 0.5
      fallback: unknown
    job_caused_by_change:
      threshold: 0.6
    pipeline_verdict:
      confidence: 0.5
      fallback: unclear
